# Agent OS — production Compose environment
# Copy to .env and fill in secrets before deploy.
# Keys are injected at container runtime — not baked into images.
# Init writes OPENCLAW_GATEWAY_TOKEN + TOOLS_API_KEY into AgentSystem.json (gateway + content-tools plugin).

# ---- Public URL ----
AGENT_OS_PUBLIC_URL=https://login.example.com
# Production Flolah: AGENT_OS_PUBLIC_URL=https://login.flolah.cloud
#   App SPA + /api          → login.<domain>
#   Marketing homepage      → apex flolah.cloud (not the login host)
#   Twenty CRM (browser UI) → crm.<domain> (dedicated subdomain; NOT marketing www/apex)
#   Optional ERP public     → https://erp.crm.<domain> (:443; Hostinger often blocks :8444)
# Legal pages (Terms / Privacy / Cookies / Open source):
#   Served from deploy/static/flolah-home/legal/ on apex and frontend/public/legal on SPA.
#   Public versions API: GET /api/auth/legal-versions
#   Versions accepted at register are stored on platform_users (terms_version / privacy_version / terms_accepted_at).
#   Bump these when published T&C/Privacy text changes (new signups must match server version when clients send it).
# AGENT_OS_TERMS_VERSION=2026-08-09
# AGENT_OS_PRIVACY_VERSION=2026-08-09
VITE_API_URL=/api

# Platform API access + error logging for backend: off | error | info
#   off   — no platform API logs
#   error — 5xx access lines + unhandled errors only
#   info  — every API request/response + errors (default)
PLATFORM_LOG_LEVEL=info

# Optional: A2A secured access-token TTL (seconds). Default 3600.
# A2A_ACCESS_TOKEN_TTL_SEC=3600
# Optional A2A invoke timing (milliseconds):
# A2A_SYNC_TIMEOUT_MS=120000          # sync invoke hold (default 2 min)
# A2A_ASYNC_WATCH_TIMEOUT_MS=86400000 # background async task watch (default 24h)
# A2A_CALLBACK_TIMEOUT_MS=15000       # outbound callback POST timeout
# AI-employee Exchange publish uses the same /api/a2a/:publishId path; Flolah visibility is denied on public endpoints (no extra env).

# Optional summary-cache full-rebuild cadence (days; default 7 each):
# LEARNINGS_FULL_REBUILD_DAYS=7
# ORDER_LEARNINGS_FULL_REBUILD_DAYS=7
# BRAIN_HISTORY_FULL_REBUILD_DAYS=7

# ---- Gateway auth (written to AgentSystem.json at init + configure-AgentSystem-docker.js) ----
OPENCLAW_GATEWAY_TOKEN=change-me-generate-a-long-random-token
# Must stay non-empty in production. Chat API: POST http://AgentSystem:18789/v1/chat/completions
# If AgentSystem.json loses gateway.http.endpoints.chatCompletions.enabled, Agent Chat → 404/502
# while the AgentSystem container still looks healthy. Auto-repaired by:
#   ensure-AgentSystem-gateway-config.js (entrypoint) + vps-verify-AgentSystem-chat.sh (every deploy)
# Backend rewrites must use AgentSystem-config-safe.js (never strip gateway/tools/plugins/browser).

# ---- Content tools: AgentSystem plugin ↔ backend auth (required for COO/MCP/kanban tools) ----
# Must match plugins.entries['agent-os-content-tools'].config.apiKey written at init.
# Generate: node ../scripts/ensure-tools-api-key.js --env-file .env --skip-AgentSystem
TOOLS_API_KEY=change-me-generate-a-long-random-secret

# Backend tool self-dispatch (POST /api/tools/invoke → tool endpoint).
# Must be loopback inside the backend container — public HTTPS (self-signed / hairpin) fails as "fetch failed".
TOOLS_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3001

# Dedicated AgentSystem agent id for backend CDP browser invokes (browse_* / job portal).
# Must match configure-AgentSystem-docker.js — profile=coding + alsoAllow browser; chat agents deny native browser.
# BROWSER_TASK_CDP_AGENT_ID=browser-cdp

# Agent Chat tool chips: also read native AgentSystem tools (browser/image/cron) from
# shared OPENCLAW_DIR session .jsonl (backend mounts openclaw_home). Optional limits:
# CHAT_OPENCLAW_SESSION_FILES=10
# CHAT_OPENCLAW_SESSION_MAX_BYTES=12582912


# Local Browser Worker (Connectors -> Browser Session package)
# Cloud-side job timeouts / offline detection only.
# Laptop .env (in the zip) keeps BROWSER_HEADLESS=0 and BROWSER_USER_DATA_DIR=browser-profile.
# Change BROWSER_USER_DATA_DIR on the laptop to use a different persistent Chromium profile (sign in again).
# BROWSER_WORKER_OFFLINE_MS=90000
# BROWSER_WORKER_JOB_TIMEOUT_MS=120000
# Full package embeds portable Node (same DESKTOP_NODE_* cache as workflow Download for Windows).
# DESKTOP_PACKAGE_SKIP_NODE_RUNTIME=0

# Video content pack (S4/S5) — optional overrides (ffmpeg is in the backend image by default)
# VIDEO_FLOW_START_URL=https://labs.google/fx/tools/flow
# VIDEO_FLOW_TEST_FIXTURES=0
# FFMPEG_PATH=ffmpeg


# ---- Internal service auth (workflow runner, tools proxy, cron-callback) ----
# Required in production — must be stable across container restarts (not ephemeral).
# Auto-generated by ./scripts/up.sh if empty. Or:
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
AGENT_OS_INTERNAL_TOKEN=

# ---- Platform admin ----
AGENT_OS_ADMIN_EMAIL=admin@agent-os.local
AGENT_OS_ADMIN_PASSWORD=change-me-admin-password

# ---- AgentSystem gateway + backend: OpenAI-compatible primary ----
# Production default: DeepSeek V4 Flash. Swap BASE_URL / MODEL / KEY for OpenAI or another host.
OPENAI_API_KEY=
OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://api.deepseek.com/v1

# Per-CEO API Keys vault (Management → API Keys). Required when users set an encryption phrase.
# Also encrypts MCP OAuth App client_secret (platform + CEO override) and vaulted OAuth tokens.
# Generate: openssl rand -hex 32  (up.sh may auto-fill if empty)
USER_API_KEYS_KEK=

# Aliases (optional — used if OPENAI_API_KEY / OPENAI_BASE_URL not set)
# OPENAI_PRIMARY_API_KEY=
OPENAI_PRIMARY_BASE_URL=https://api.deepseek.com/v1
OPENAI_PRIMARY_MODEL=deepseek-v4-flash

# AgentSystem default agent model slug (written to openclaw.json at init).
# Must exist in models.providers.openai.models (id without the openai/ prefix).
# After a container recreate, ensure-openclaw-gateway-config.js restores an empty
# catalog from bak; vps-verify-openclaw-chat.sh re-runs configure if still empty.
OPENCLAW_MODEL_PRIMARY=openai/deepseek-v4-flash

# Optional comma-separated AgentSystem model fallbacks (e.g. openai/gpt-4o-mini).
# Leave empty unless you intentionally want failover (do not point at ollama/* for production COO).
OPENCLAW_MODEL_FALLBACKS=

# Ollama as AgentSystem silent fallback (default off — tool calling is unreliable on small local models)
# Set to 1 only for experiments; configure-AgentSystem-docker.js clears fallbacks when unset/0
OPENCLAW_ENABLE_OLLAMA_FALLBACK=0

# ---- Anthropic (AgentSystem gateway — e.g. anthropic/claude-opus-4-6) ----
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=

# ---- Secondary OpenAI-compatible endpoint (optional; Admin "Use secondary") ----
# OPENAI_SECONDARY_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
# OPENAI_SECONDARY_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_SECONDARY_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini
# Or another OpenAI-compatible host:
# OPENAI_SECONDARY_BASE_URL=https://api.deepseek.com/v1
# OPENAI_SECONDARY_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_SECONDARY_MODEL=deepseek-chat

# ---- CEO Profile BYOK chat model fallbacks (when llm_model not yet set) ----
# Profile UI asks CEOs to pick provider + model; AgentSystem sync uses that choice.
# Internal endpoint map: openai → api.openai.com, openrouter → openrouter.ai, etc.
# These env vars are soft fallbacks only (never inherit OPENAI_PRIMARY_MODEL=deepseek-* for OpenAI BYOK).
# OPENAI_BYOK_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini
# OPENROUTER_MODEL=openai/gpt-4o-mini
# Catalog: GET /api/auth/llm-catalog  (backend/src/config/llm-provider-registry.js)

# ---- Ollama (AgentSystem optional-ollama profile + BYOK Free) ----
OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://ollama:11434
OLLAMA_API_KEY=ollama-local
# Default pull / BYOK Free model (compose + backend)
OLLAMA_MODEL=llama3.2
# Context window for Ollama provider config (code default 32768; avoid 128k on small VPS RAM)
OLLAMA_CONTEXT_WINDOW=32768
# Alias used when wiring AgentSystem silent ollama fallback (only if ENABLE_OLLAMA_FALLBACK=1)
OPENCLAW_OLLAMA_FALLBACK_MODEL=llama3.2
# Optional: longer gateway timeout for slow local models (ms)
# OPENCLAW_OLLAMA_CHAT_TIMEOUT_MS=300000

# ---- Brave Search (agent tool + optional platform MCP) ----
# Deploy operators: set SKIP_PLATFORM_MCPS=1 to only write env keys (no container build/seed)
# for Brave + Meta Graph + Business Core MCPs (vps-deploy-latest.sh / ensure-platform-mcps.sh).
# SKIP_PLATFORM_MCPS=0
# Agent content tool brave_web_search: Platform default Profile uses BRAVE_API_KEY;
# any other Profile LLM uses vault BRAVE_SEARCH_BYOK only (no platform fall-back).
# Platform MCP mcp-brave-search (profile optional-brave-mcp): header BYOK only —
# MCP container does NOT use BRAVE_API_KEY. ensure-platform-mcps.sh starts + seeds.
# Get a key: https://api-dashboard.search.brave.com/app/keys
# Manual: docker compose --profile optional-brave-mcp up -d --build brave-search-mcp
#         docker compose exec backend node scripts/seed-brave-search-mcp.js
BRAVE_API_KEY=
BRAVE_MCP_URL=http://brave-search-mcp:8080/mcp
# Tool: brave_web_search (agent content tool + MCP wrapper).

# ---- Google Places API (New) + Social Research ----
# Agent tools google_places_* / business_discover: Platform default uses GOOGLE_PLACES_API_KEY
# (falls back to vault GOOGLE_PLACES_BYOK if unset); any other Profile LLM uses vault only.
# Enable Places API (New) on the Google Cloud project. Nearby Search does not use nextPageToken in FieldMask.
# MCP mcp-social-research (profile optional-social-research-mcp) + Instaloader sidecar.
# FLOLAH_EXCHANGE_PUBLISHER_USER_ID = CEO who owns the default Flolah Exchange listings
#   (Social Researcher, Business Discovery). Defaults to the first enabled CEO.
# Manual: docker compose --profile optional-social-research-mcp up -d --build instaloader-sidecar social-research-mcp
#         docker compose exec backend node scripts/seed-social-research-mcp.js
#         docker compose exec backend node scripts/seed-social-research-agents.js
# Test:   bash deploy/scripts/vps-smoke-social-research.sh
# Business Discovery: Discover → Research → Track → Act. Research does not persist unless asked.
GOOGLE_PLACES_API_KEY=
INSTALOADER_URL=http://instaloader-sidecar:8083
SOCIAL_RESEARCH_MCP_URL=http://social-research-mcp:8084/mcp
# Optional: Instagram sessionid cookie for Instaloader (prefer per-CEO vault INSTAGRAM_SESSIONID).
# INSTAGRAM_SESSIONID=
# Sidecar is self-hosted. Anonymous instagram.com calls from this VPS return HTTP 429 (not 409).
# Leave 0 unless debugging Instaloader without a cookie.
# INSTALOADER_ALLOW_ANONYMOUS=0
# Optional: X API v2 bearer for official timelines (prefer vault X_API_BYOK when Profile ≠ platform default).
# Tweet text/media hydration from status URLs works without this key.
# X_BEARER_TOKEN=
# FLOLAH_EXCHANGE_PUBLISHER_USER_ID=

# ---- Facebook / Meta Graph (platform MCP + Connectors → MCPs OAuth) ----
# Platform MCP mcp-meta-graph (profile optional-meta-graph-mcp).
# Platform App credentials (admin default) — CEOs may override App ID/secret in UI.
# Per-CEO OAuth *access* after Connect; secrets encrypted with USER_API_KEYS_KEK.
# ensure-platform-mcps.sh starts container + seeds registry + oauth provider defaults.
# Manual: docker compose --profile optional-meta-graph-mcp up -d --build meta-graph-mcp
#         docker compose exec backend node scripts/seed-meta-graph-mcp.js
# Docs: knowledgebase/platform-help/31-mcp-connectors-oauth.md
# FACEBOOK_APP_ID=
# FACEBOOK_APP_SECRET=
META_GRAPH_MCP_URL=http://meta-graph-mcp:8081/mcp

# ---- Business Core MCP (CRM/ERP for workflows; profile optional-business-core-mcp) ----
# ensure-platform-mcps.sh starts + seeds mcp-flolah-crm / mcp-flolah-erp.
# Manual: docker compose --profile optional-business-core-mcp up -d --build business-core-mcp
#         docker compose exec backend node scripts/seed-business-core-mcp.js
# Docs: knowledgebase/platform-help/32-business-core-crm-erp.md
BUSINESS_CORE_MCP_URL=http://business-core-mcp:8082/mcp

# Optional: after vps-deploy-latest, re-seed content-publish-social + content-comments-ingest
# for this CEO (workflow nodes + Meta Graph MCP). Brains use vault Platform_BYOK when set.
# SEED_CONTENT_MEDIA_OWNER=ceo-content-api-phase01-057515
# SKIP_CONTENT_MEDIA_SEED=0
# CONTENT_COMMENTS_BRAIN_KEY_REF=Platform_BYOK
# Video content studio Phase 1 (agents + W-Reasoning from standard/video-content):
#   WORKFLOW_SEED_OWNER_ID=ceo-bala node backend/scripts/seed-video-content-workflows.js
#   REFRESH_WORKFLOWS_ONLY=1 node backend/scripts/seed-video-content-workflows.js
#   WORKFLOW_SEED_OWNER_ID=ceo-bala node backend/scripts/test-video-content-phase1.js
#   node backend/scripts/test-video-storyboard-ceo-approval.js
# Update Company Details (avatar -> /update-company-details): no extra env; uses CEO session + company_memory Knowledge table.
# Company industry blueprints (Admin publish / export.zip) need no extra env secrets.
# Snapshot + publish live in: company-blueprint-publish.js + company-blueprints/registry.js.
# Secrets: secret-sanitize.js always redacts live API keys / bridge tokens / passwords on
# Admin snapshot, publish, JSON inspect, and zip export (vault *Ref + {{templates}} kept).
# Shared ops MD fallback (when agent lacks AGENT-OS-OPS.md): AgentSystem-workspace-templates/_shared/.
# Ops: docker compose exec backend node scripts/validate-company-blueprint-export.mjs (DRY_RUN=1)
#      docker compose exec backend node scripts/republish-content-ops-blueprint.js
# Public callback (defaults to AGENT_OS_BASE_URL + /api/integrations/mcp/oauth/callback)
# MCP_OAUTH_CALLBACK_URL=https://login.example.com/api/integrations/mcp/oauth/callback

# ---- OpenRouter (backend dev/scripts; Brain nodes use per-node keys in workflow editor) ----
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# OPENROUTER_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
# OPENROUTER_MODEL=openai/gpt-4o-mini
# OPENROUTER_HTTP_REFERER=https://your-app.example.com
# OPENROUTER_SITE_TITLE=Agent OS

# ---- DeepSeek via local Ollama (no cloud API key) ----
# Requires: docker compose --profile optional-ollama up -d ollama
# Preferred model: deepseek-v3 (needs large GPU/RAM host).
# Small VPS auto-fallback: deepseek-r1:8b (ensure-deepseek-env.sh)
# DEEPSEEK_BASE_URL=http://ollama:11434/v1
# DEEPSEEK_MODEL=deepseek-v3
# DEEPSEEK_FALLBACK_MODEL=deepseek-r1:8b
# ensure-deepseek-env.sh may write this host note when the full model is skipped:
# DEEPSEEK_NOTE=full deepseek-v3 skipped on this host (set DEEPSEEK_MODEL=deepseek-v3 on a large GPU box)

# ---- Backend LLM overrides ----
# OPENAI_COO_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini
# OPENAI_INTENT_MODEL=
# TOOLS_SUMMARIZE_MODEL=

# ---- Content tools: image (OpenAI-compatible / GPT-image) ----
# Primary reuses OPENAI_PRIMARY_* / OPENAI_API_KEY above.
TOOLS_IMAGE_MODEL=gpt-image-1
TOOLS_IMAGE_SIZE=1024x1024
TOOLS_IMAGE_QUALITY=medium
TOOLS_IMAGE_STYLE=natural
TOOLS_IMAGE_MAX_PROMPT_CHARS=1000
# TOOLS_IMAGE_SECONDARY_MODEL=gpt-image-1-mini

# ---- Content tools: analyze_image (vision / OCR) ----
# Tool name: analyze_image. Platform default uses the same effective platform LLM as chat
# (Admin primary/secondary switch). BYOK Profiles use vault Platform_BYOK + Profile primary.
# Optional ops override (rare):
# TOOLS_VISION_MODEL=
# TOOLS_VISION_BASE_URL=
# TOOLS_VISION_API_KEY=
# TOOLS_VISION_MAX_TOKENS=1200
# TOOLS_VISION_MAX_MB=15

# ---- Content tools: Replicate video ----
REPLICATE_API_TOKEN=

# ElevenLabs (workflow ElevenLabs node TTS/STT). Avatar templates default vault key name "elevenlabs-key".
# AVATAR_MODEL_MAX_MB=80
ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=

# Free local STT/TTS — Compose profile optional-voice (started by ensure-voice-env.sh on deploy).
# Used by Agent Chat mic, workflow speech_* nodes, and COO content tools speech_tts / speech_stt.
# SKIP_VOICE=1 on deploy to skip containers. Defaults written by ensure-voice-env.sh if missing:
SPEECH_STT_URL=http://whisper:8000
SPEECH_TTS_URL=http://piper:5500
WHISPER_MODEL=Systran/faster-whisper-tiny.en
PIPER_VOICE=en_US-lessac-medium
# WHISPER_IMAGE=fedirz/faster-whisper-server:latest-cpu
# Generated media (/api/media/AgentSystem/...) requires login by default.
# WhatsApp attaches via MEDIA:/abs/path on the shared AgentSystem volume — do not enable public signed URLs unless required.
# MEDIA_PUBLIC_SIGNED=1
# MEDIA_SIGNING_SECRET=

# Hunyuan3D optional GPU service (profile optional-hunyuan3d)
# HUNYUAN3D_URL=http://hunyuan3d:7860
# HUNYUAN3D_IMAGE=tencent/hunyuan3d:2.1
# HUNYUAN3D_TIMEOUT_MS=900000
REPLICATE_PRIMARY_BASE_URL=https://api.replicate.com/v1
# Platform Replicate token (optional). Non-platform CEOs use vault Replicate_BYOK for video_media_generate / generate_video.
# REPLICATE_API_TOKEN=
# TOOLS_VIDEO_MODEL_VERSION=owner/model:version_id
# TOOLS_VIDEO_MAX_PROMPT_CHARS=500
# REPLICATE_SECONDARY_API_TOKEN=
# TOOLS_VIDEO_SECONDARY_MODEL_VERSION=
# REPLICATE_SECONDARY_BASE_URL=

# ---- Job Applicant / browser timeouts (ms) ----
OPENCLAW_DISCOVERY_TIMEOUT_MS=900000
# Recommended when agents use browse_task_status wait_ms (up to 90000).
OPENCLAW_FETCH_TIMEOUT_MS=360000

# ---- Scheduled jobs (crons) — platform-level timers, per-user effect ----
# Every value has a built-in default; all keys are OPTIONAL and shown commented for reference.
# One timer runs per backend process; each tick loops over enabled CEOs / their own rows, so
# per-user settings (standup scheduled_at, workflow schedule_cron, data_retention_days) still apply.
# Full reference: knowledgebase/platform-help/19-scheduled-jobs-and-crons.md
# deploy/scripts/ensure-cron-env.sh appends this same block to deploy/.env on every deploy.
#
# STANDUP_SCHEDULE_CRON=* * * * *          # dispatcher: runs each user standup at its own scheduled_at
# STANDUP_CRON_SCHEDULE=                   # legacy auto-collect standup for every CEO (empty = disabled)
# DELEGATION_CRON_SCHEDULE=* * * * *       # process pending COO -> agent delegation tasks, per CEO
# DELEGATION_STATUS_ONLY_MAX_RETRIES=1      # auto-requeue when agent only posts "marked completed" (0–3)
# DELEGATION_GATEWAY_MAX_RETRIES=8         # leave delegation pending on AgentSystem unreachable (cap)
# STATUS_ONLY_REQUEUE_STARTUP_DELAY_MS=60000  # wait after boot before stuck status-only requeue
# AGENT_WORKFLOW_SCHEDULER_CRON=* * * * *  # master tick: runs user workflows whose schedule_cron is due
# JOB_PIPELINE_CRON_SCHEDULE=0 * * * *     # Job Applicant pipeline tick across active job profiles
# COO_STATUS_CHECKER_CRON=0 9 * * *        # daily CEO status report -> standup chat + HTML email
# DATA_RETENTION_CRON=15 3 * * *           # daily purge: chats/standup msgs/workflow runs + aged Content Explorer media (hard delete)
# KANBAN_ORPHAN_WATCHER_CRON=*/5 * * * *   # re-pend stuck processing + reinitiate orphan specialty Kanban + workflow stuck-step renudge
# KANBAN_ORPHAN_MAX_RETRIES=2              # cap automatic reinitiates per card (default 2)
# WORKFLOW_STUCK_HARD_HOURS=24             # hard renudge workflow steps open this long (accurate soft rules for agent dels use specialty stale window)
# WORKFLOW_COO_WAKE_ON_TERMINAL=1          # re-invoke COO after async workflow terminal (multi-phase CRM→ERP). Set 0 to disable.
# DELEGATION_SPECIALTY_PROCESSING_TIMEOUT_MS=600000  # specialty "processing" older than this → re-pend (default 10m)
# SCHEDULED_GOALS_CRON=* * * * *          # CEO scheduled goals: hourly|daily|weekdays|weekly prompts → AI employee (pause/delete off)
# GOAL_PLAN_MAX_SPECIALTY=8              # Max specialist intents per durable goal plan (multi-intent specialty_task steps; chat COO still max 2)
# GOAL_PLAN_COMPLETION_NUDGE_CRON=*/10 * * * *  # Admin event watcher: backfill goal completion chat nudge
# GOAL_PLAN_COO_COMPLETION_NUDGE=1              # On plan completed/failed: once-only COO chat status + bell (0 hard-disables; Admin pause also)
# GOAL_PLAN_COO_NUDGE_TIMEOUT_MS=45000          # Max wait for optional COO LLM wording before deterministic ladder fallback
# GOAL_PLAN_FAILURE_KANBAN=1                    # 0 disables recovery Kanban+delegation when a plan fails (must be in docker-compose backend-env)
# GOAL_AGENT_CONTINUE_TIMEOUT_MS=240000       # AgentSystem agent_continue timeout for goal-plan interpretation steps
# SCHEDULED_GOAL_CHAT_TIMEOUT_MS=240000       # Chat-mode scheduled goal AgentSystem timeout
# WORKFLOW_TERMINAL_WATCH_CRON=*/5 * * * *       # Admin event watcher: re-advance stuck goal steps after WF terminal
# WORKFLOW_COO_WAKE_ON_TERMINAL=1               # 0 disables COO re-invoke on WF terminal
# WORKFLOW_TIMEOUT_WATCHDOG_CRON=*/1 * * * *    # Admin event watcher: reap timed-out workflow steps
# REGRESSION_GOAL_PLAN=1                 # Full regression includes adhoc CRM+ERP+Help+notify goal plan e2e (0 to skip)
# REGRESSION_GOAL_PLAN_FORCE_TERMINAL=1  # Force-complete child WF/specialty terminals in goal-plan e2e (no live CEO gates)
# Multiphase CRM→ERP freeform: agent_workflow_trigger with ≥2 planned workflows (no goal_run_id) auto-upgrades to agent_goal_create (agr-…).
# Major goals: agent_goal_create returns async:true + plan_summary; platform advances steps on child terminal (watch notifies include agr-… + title when bound).
# Chat: new multiphase CEO ask → new agr-… by default (COO AGENTS/SOUL). Scheduled plan-mode tick/Run now → new agr-… each fire (approved plan_json = step template only).
# Terminal: completeGoalRun → one COO completion chat bubble (context_json.coo_completion_nudge_at) so CEO need not re-enquire; chat soft-polls while agr-… visible.
# Optional direct: docker exec … node scripts/test-goal-plan-async-ui.mjs  (or backend npm run test:goal-plan:async-ui)

# CRM_TLS_WORKSPACE_CERT_CRON=40 * * * *   # expand LE SANs when ACTIVE Twenty {sub}.crm.* missing from cert (Admin → Crons)
# CRM_TLS_WORKSPACE_CERT_AUTO=1            # 0 = skip post-provision debounce; CRM_TLS_WORKSPACE_CERT_CRON=off disables schedule
# CRM_TLS_WORKSPACE_CERT_DEBOUNCE_MS=45000 # wait after new workspace before SAN expand

# ---- AgentSystem channel media caps (configure-AgentSystem-docker.js) ----
# OPENCLAW_MEDIA_MAX_MB=128

# ---- Custom workflow scripts (Python/JS sandbox in backend container) ----
# CUSTOM_SCRIPT_MAX_BYTES=131072
# CUSTOM_SCRIPT_TIMEOUT_MS=60000
# CUSTOM_SCRIPT_PYTHON=python3
# CUSTOM_SCRIPT_NODE=node
# LLM security review at registration (uses OPENAI_* / Ollama above — same as backend LLM)
# CUSTOM_SCRIPT_LLM_REVIEW=1
# CUSTOM_SCRIPT_LLM_REVIEW_REQUIRED=1
# CUSTOM_SCRIPT_LLM_REVIEW_MAX_TOKENS=768

# ---- Workflow email + MFA + email_send content tool ----
# Used by: workflow Send Email node, email_send tool (incl. ICS calendar invites), MFA email OTP
# notify_ceo (in-app CEO push / NotificationBell) needs no SMTP — granted at backend boot
